## Quick Guide to Building

For new users, the Quick Start chapter in the User Manual contains a detailed Quick Start guide. Download the User Manual:

  <@RELEASE_URL@/docs/rtems-@RELEASE@-user.pdf>

and follow the instructions in the Quick Start section. If you are familiar with RTEMS or just want to get going, the following steps will download the RTEMS Source Builder:

```sh
cd
mkdir -p development/rtems
cd development/rtems
wget @RELEASE_URL@/sources/rtems-source-builder-@RELEASE@.tar.xz
tar Jxf rtems-source-builder-@RELEASE@.tar.xz
cd rtems-source-builder-@RELEASE@/rtems
```

To build the tools for the ARM architecture:

```sh
../source-builder/sb-set-builder   --prefix=$HOME/development/rtems/@RELEASE@   @VERSION@/rtems-arm
```

To build the tools, kernel and all packages for the BeagleBone Black:

```sh
../source-builder/sb-set-builder   --prefix=$HOME/development/rtems/@RELEASE@   bsps/beagleboneblack
```

If you encounter a problem, please drop by our Discord server (<https://www.rtems.org/discord>) or post to <https://users.rtems.org/>.

If you find a bug, please raise an issue at <https://gitlab.rtems.org/rtems/>.
